profile: minimodel-mirust.taboo.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
site: MiniModel.MiRust.com
role: prohibited directions

memory_endpoints_two_use_context:
  - Direct use: ecosystem agents use MemoryEndpoints.com for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across all sites.
  - Separate plugin use: a TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  - Lane boundary: keep identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate; neither lane silently acts for the other.

prohibitions:
  - Do not describe MiniModel.org as a model host, inference service, conversion service, model-byte proxy, or quality authority.
  - Do not infer current peer availability, public reachability, qualification, deployment, or publication from metadata, source, local probes, fixtures, or mocks.
  - Do not retain obsolete formats, compatibility paths, aliases, fallback, hidden retry, or text handoffs as acquisition.
  - Do not describe MemoryEndpoints.com as unauthorized, disconnected, or outside the ecosystem plan.
  - Do not conflate the direct agent lane with the user plugin lane, share credentials or consent across lanes, or let either lane silently act for the other.
  - Do not silently upload prompts, transcripts, local memory, meeting content, credentials, invitation URLs, tokens, model bytes, or raw hosted-memory payloads.
  - Do not let redundant prelaunch memory copies drift or contradict one another; keep every maintained copy current, secret-safe, and provenance-labeled.
  - Do not deploy from dirty, partially tested, ambiguous, stale, or undocumented source.
